## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of runtime extensibility, concurrency, and observable behavior in production telemetry systems.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern with a pluggable registry
- Thread-safety and lock-free reads
- Reservoir, probabilistic, and adaptive sampling trade-offs
- Deterministic testing via seedable RNG

## Code Example

```javascript
interface SamplingContext {
  // e.g., current rate, throughput, tenant, etc.
  rate: number
}
interface SamplingStrategy {
  name: string
  shouldEmit(ctx: SamplingContext): boolean
}
class StrategyRegistry {
  private registry = new Map<string, () => SamplingStrategy>()
  register(name: string, factory: () => SamplingStrategy) {
    this.registry.set(name, factory)
  }
  get(name: string): SamplingStrategy {
    const factory = this.registry.get(name)
    return factory ? factory() : defaultStrategy()
  }
}
function ReservoirStrategy(k: number): SamplingStrategy { return { name: 'Reservoir', shouldEmit: ctx => keepSample(ctx, k) } }
function ProbabilisticStrategy(p: number): SamplingStrategy { return { name: 'Probabilistic', shouldEmit: ctx => Math.random() < p } }
function AdaptiveStrategy(targetRate: number): SamplingStrategy { return { name: 'Adaptive', shouldEmit: ctx => adapt(ctx, targetRate) } }
```

